Yeah - that looks plausible.<br><br>If this is the right place in the code then the nonlinearity appears to be coming from the two sets of GEN_set_min and GEN_set_max calls which appear to be clamping 'total' to within +/- limit but doing so independently along the two axes.  So I think it would suffice to say that if one axis needs to be clamped then the other must be reduced by the same proportion...or perhaps don't do the clamp unless both axes need to be clamped...it's hard to say which is right.<br><br>Well, at least that gives me a place to start digging.<br><br>Many thanks!<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=726">SteveBaker</a> — Mon Aug 14, 2006 1:39 am</p><hr />
